00:56:22.230 --> 00:56:22.950
I, um...

00:56:24.540 --> 00:56:26.010
I look simply full.

00:56:26.630 --> 00:56:26.950
Exactly.

00:56:27.630 --> 00:56:29.900
Right, where were you?

00:56:30.940 --> 00:56:34.700
I don't need a guardian every afternoon.

00:56:34.940 --> 00:56:36.240
No, you need a regiment.

00:56:36.600 --> 00:56:39.140
Well, Father, can I prevent him skating if he wants to?

00:56:39.560 --> 00:56:41.340
I can, that Mephisto.

00:56:41.830 --> 00:56:46.090
I'll prevent his skating, I'll prevent his kissing, I'll prevent his living.

00:56:46.620 --> 00:56:48.380
That's enough. You'll do nothing of the kind.

00:56:48.760 --> 00:56:51.180
You go on back to your rooms. Both you girls, back to your rooms. Go on.

00:56:51.800 --> 00:56:53.820
From now on, I'll handle this matter myself.

00:57:03.230 --> 00:57:05.890
He's an hour late for dress rehearsal. And what is he anyway? In English?

00:57:06.180 --> 00:57:08.300
Yes. Think that I, who made him, created him.

00:57:08.640 --> 00:57:11.420
Lifted him up from a mere nobody to a great star.

00:57:12.720 --> 00:57:15.980
And overnight, facing every newspaper, his name in lights.

00:57:16.180 --> 00:57:17.320
It was I. I.

00:57:17.480 --> 00:57:19.780
So it was you. You were the fellow who kissed the girl in the cinema, huh?

00:57:20.690 --> 00:57:24.440
Yes. No. Remind me to remind Martha to do it again.

00:57:34.700 --> 00:57:36.900
I'm a respectable woman, I tell you I am.

00:57:37.320 --> 00:57:38.380
I admit it.

00:57:38.800 --> 00:57:40.620
In fact, I'm in favor of it.

00:57:42.520 --> 00:57:46.020
Oh, but I can't stand this concealment anymore.

00:57:46.910 --> 00:57:47.610
Can't you believe it?

00:57:47.750 --> 00:57:48.070
No.

00:57:48.960 --> 00:57:52.740
Either we must face your husband, or we must part.

00:57:53.800 --> 00:57:55.080
In the first period...

00:57:55.680 --> 00:57:56.920
What is there left to do?

00:58:00.160 --> 00:58:07.440
Yes, I understand, but how will I ever forgive myself for biting your heart?

00:58:08.100 --> 00:58:11.640
Oh, that's all right, little woman.

00:58:19.960 --> 00:58:20.280
Him?

00:58:21.540 --> 00:58:25.020
Yes, it doesn't make any difference. It's a girl.

00:58:25.510 --> 00:58:25.910
Goodbye.

00:58:27.360 --> 00:58:29.760
Yes, I know how you are suffering, Philip.

00:58:31.280 --> 00:58:32.360
You are suffering, aren't you?

00:58:32.640 --> 00:58:33.550
What? Why?

00:58:34.110 --> 00:58:34.570
Naturally.

00:58:36.340 --> 00:58:41.850
Well, if we are saying goodbye, you may kiss me for the last time.

00:58:42.540 --> 00:58:44.560
You mean for the first time?

00:59:01.120 --> 00:59:02.440
Good morning. Did you have a good rest?

00:59:02.620 --> 00:59:03.240
Yes, thank you.

00:59:03.480 --> 00:59:06.500
I trust this dress rehearsal's not going to be too much of a strain for you.

00:59:06.640 --> 00:59:08.080
Oh, not at all. No, thank you.

00:59:08.520 --> 00:59:10.720
I thought it was going to be different, but look at this.

00:59:10.820 --> 00:59:13.360
We're just as unready as any company at a dress rehearsal.

00:59:13.580 --> 00:59:15.520
Back to your places. Come on. Move. Hurry.

00:59:16.190 --> 00:59:17.370
Move like snails.

00:59:17.790 --> 00:59:19.820
Snails. Shut up. I know my lines.

00:59:20.250 --> 00:59:22.130
Okay, I just want you to run over the new lyrics to the song.

00:59:22.520 --> 00:59:25.400
And put some warmth and some oomph into it, you know.

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:30.520
I was slipping.

00:59:30.760 --> 00:59:31.890
I was slipping.

00:59:32.330 --> 00:59:34.730
And so I thought to see a movie would be a reference.

00:59:34.850 --> 00:59:35.470
Yes, that's fine.

00:59:35.630 --> 00:59:36.210
Splendid, excellent.

00:59:36.960 --> 00:59:38.780
But more warmth, my dear boy.

00:59:38.920 --> 00:59:39.680
More mmmm.

00:59:41.070 --> 00:59:42.870
Apparently, I haven't so much mmmm.

00:59:44.080 --> 00:59:45.280
Now, I'm going to show you how to do it.

00:59:45.930 --> 00:59:46.970
I'm going to play you.

00:59:47.300 --> 00:59:48.960
Oh, that's a bad piece of casting.

00:59:49.840 --> 00:59:51.420
Well, I'll be you for the time being.

00:59:52.130 --> 00:59:55.390
Now, I'm going to sing the song that all Paris is waiting to hear.

00:59:55.630 --> 00:59:59.910
And you must imagine me coming down the aisle and taking my seat just as you did in the cinema of the famous Kiss.

01:00:00.280 --> 01:00:01.320
And you'll sit next to Clara.

01:00:01.540 --> 01:00:02.820
Clara? Clara, yes.

01:00:04.030 --> 01:00:06.430
Clara is going to play the Penelon girl, you see.

01:00:06.510 --> 01:00:07.910
Another bad piece of casting.

01:00:08.190 --> 01:00:09.790
How do you know? You've never kissed me.

01:00:10.010 --> 01:00:10.590
Well, I did.

01:00:12.060 --> 01:00:13.100
Why at Poo Poo?

01:00:15.140 --> 01:00:16.260
Come, come, come, come, come.

01:00:16.460 --> 01:00:17.720
Now, this is how it must be sung.

01:00:18.280 --> 01:00:22.960
The mask of comedy concealing the throbbing heart of romance.

01:00:23.860 --> 01:00:24.900
You follow me. It'll be quite easy.

01:00:25.500 --> 01:00:26.180
My key, please.

01:00:27.650 --> 01:00:29.610
Now, the first part's unimportant, you see, because...

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:36.680
tells a story and everybody knows the story so uh all right you know the rain was dripping and i

01:00:36.680 --> 01:00:41.500
was slipping and so i thought to see a movie would be ripping it was a doctor so nice to park there

01:00:41.500 --> 01:00:49.360
especially on that rainy afternoon a lovely stranger sat there beside me and there was danger

01:00:49.360 --> 01:00:57.310
but no conscience there to guide me i squeezed her hand then it was so grand then on that lucky rain

01:00:57.310 --> 01:00:58.530
Rain, rain, rainy afternoon

01:01:00.860 --> 01:01:02.840
There was a scene of love supreme, but in between

01:01:02.840 --> 01:01:07.510
I caught a glimpse of loveliness divine

01:01:08.010 --> 01:01:10.890
That stole away this heart of mine

01:01:10.890 --> 01:01:14.920
Believe me, mister, who could resist her?

01:01:15.460 --> 01:01:18.740
Before I knew what I was doing, I had kissed her

01:01:19.310 --> 01:01:25.570
There's another way to do that. You can kiss her before you sing the words.

01:01:25.610 --> 01:01:26.450
We'll try that again.

01:01:26.940 --> 01:01:29.900
Before I knew what I was doing, I had...

01:01:30.640 --> 01:01:31.140
Kissed her?

01:01:31.620 --> 01:01:36.210
I think it's better to kiss her after you say the word kissed her.

01:01:36.250 --> 01:01:37.390
It gives you a little more time.

01:01:37.510 --> 01:01:37.970
Don't you want?

01:01:38.560 --> 01:01:42.400
Before I knew what I was doing, I had kissed her.

01:01:50.120 --> 01:01:50.300
What?

01:01:50.590 --> 01:01:50.810
Well, yeah.

01:01:52.190 --> 01:01:53.110
Stories simple.

01:01:54.310 --> 01:01:55.270
Tossy dimple.

01:01:56.320 --> 01:01:58.320
Together on that rainy afternoon.

01:02:05.500 --> 01:02:06.840
You did that very well, Martijn, very well.

01:02:08.920 --> 01:02:11.040
Oh, uh, shall I try it again?

01:02:11.530 --> 01:02:12.270
Again, if you like, yeah.

01:02:12.800 --> 01:02:13.640
All right, come on, Clara.

01:02:14.060 --> 01:02:15.320
No, no, no, no, Clara's busy.

01:02:15.990 --> 01:02:18.050
Lulu, you come and understand the colors from Mr. Martijn, will you?

01:02:19.380 --> 01:02:20.780
How long have you been employed in my theater?

01:02:28.400 --> 01:02:28.620
Yeah?

01:02:30.060 --> 01:02:30.420
What are you looking for?

01:02:30.580 --> 01:02:31.100
How do you do?

01:02:31.750 --> 01:02:32.770
Is it about Monique?

01:02:32.950 --> 01:02:34.010
So, you call her Monique, do you?

01:02:35.130 --> 01:02:36.250
I can't explain that.

01:02:36.370 --> 01:02:36.590
That's all.

01:02:36.670 --> 01:02:37.590
I'm not here for an explanation.

01:02:37.750 --> 01:02:39.010
This friendship, if that's what you call it,

01:02:39.070 --> 01:02:39.450
Masise!

01:02:41.730 --> 01:02:42.670
Sorry to hear that.

01:02:43.330 --> 01:02:46.240
You see, I am deeply indebted to your daughter,

01:02:46.710 --> 01:02:49.520
but as much as I would like it to be otherwise,

01:02:50.200 --> 01:02:52.380
our friendship is nothing but a business arrangement.

01:02:52.980 --> 01:02:53.300
Business?

01:02:53.700 --> 01:02:53.900
Yes.

01:02:54.360 --> 01:02:56.720
You see, after she paid my fine and got me out of jail,

01:02:57.170 --> 01:02:58.910
well, the least I could do was to pay her back.

01:02:59.650 --> 01:02:59.970
Monique!

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:01.260
Did she pay your fine?

01:03:02.440 --> 01:03:03.460
Yes. Why, a fine?

01:03:20.500 --> 01:03:22.780
Now, look here, my friend. I want to hear more about this.

01:03:22.860 --> 01:03:23.920
Why did she pay your fine?

01:03:24.370 --> 01:03:26.990
You see, she realized that as long as I was in jail,

01:03:27.110 --> 01:03:29.130
the whole incident would be headlined in the papers.

01:03:29.550 --> 01:03:29.910
So...

01:03:32.200 --> 01:03:34.440
I'm only interested in there being no more scandal.

01:03:34.660 --> 01:03:37.500
And as you are a gentleman that respects Monique...

01:03:37.500 --> 01:03:41.010
Respect? Monsieur Peller, and there's nothing in the world I wouldn't...

01:03:41.010 --> 01:03:45.730
Well, then, for Monique's sake, I hope you will use discretion, good judgment, and good taste.

01:03:46.620 --> 01:03:48.360
And no more scandal.

01:03:49.550 --> 01:03:50.230
For Monique's sake.

01:03:51.050 --> 01:03:52.150
Thank you, Martin.

01:03:54.760 --> 01:03:55.800
Goodbye, Martin!

01:04:01.500 --> 01:04:02.060
Thank you, Martin.

01:04:06.530 --> 01:04:07.430
Thank you, Gareth.

01:04:13.670 --> 01:04:13.950
Me!

01:04:14.910 --> 01:04:17.930
Fredo, I won't be followed about like this if you wanted something you could have waited.

01:04:18.090 --> 01:04:19.380
Yes, but look.

01:04:23.030 --> 01:04:23.230
Oh?

01:04:24.570 --> 01:04:25.490
You are mad at him.

01:04:25.710 --> 01:04:26.590
Oh, I'm delighted.

01:04:27.220 --> 01:04:27.800
I'll show him.

01:04:28.510 --> 01:04:29.250
Oh, precious.

01:04:29.430 --> 01:04:29.750
Monique.

01:04:30.640 --> 01:04:37.150
Monique! Oh, Monique, wait.

01:04:37.450 --> 01:04:39.780
Oh, you, you, you women in taxi cabs.

01:04:39.800 --> 01:04:40.000
Who?

01:04:40.340 --> 01:04:42.220
Just so that you can get your pictures in the paper again.

01:04:42.620 --> 01:04:44.440
What do you do, hire photographers to follow you?

01:04:44.920 --> 01:04:47.400
Oh, that was the girl I thought I was kissing in the cinema.

01:04:47.640 --> 01:04:51.520
But I was just saying goodbye to her forever so that you and I could...

01:04:53.740 --> 01:04:55.080
Look, the monster!

01:04:55.460 --> 01:04:56.500
Oh, no, no, not me.

01:04:56.580 --> 01:04:57.040
Him, him.

01:04:57.240 --> 01:04:57.760
Let it come along.

01:05:12.090 --> 01:05:13.170
What have I done?

01:05:13.580 --> 01:05:14.950
Oh, just a minute, please.

01:05:15.730 --> 01:05:17.110
Are you going to let them do this to me?

01:05:23.680 --> 01:05:24.540
No violence now.

01:05:39.370 --> 01:05:43.660
all their money back. You still had money to give them back. I still had it here. Do you realize that

01:05:43.660 --> 01:05:48.240
the curtain goes up in a few hours? Yes. And you haven't got a leading man? Ah, yes, you have.

01:05:49.140 --> 01:05:55.140
I'm in perfect voice. I have 15 years of experience behind me. Behind you? Have you ever

01:05:55.140 --> 01:05:58.660
kissed a girl in the cinema? You ever kissed one? Just one? One? One?

01:06:00.350 --> 01:06:00.830
I have it.

01:06:01.110 --> 01:06:01.850
You're his understudy.

01:06:01.910 --> 01:06:03.150
You've been understudy behind the bars.

01:06:03.410 --> 01:06:03.670
Bah!

01:06:04.300 --> 01:06:05.640
I am no convict.

01:06:05.840 --> 01:06:06.740
And you're no singer.

01:06:06.940 --> 01:06:07.860
But you're a prompter.

01:06:08.000 --> 01:06:09.460
It's your job to think things up.

01:06:09.940 --> 01:06:11.320
We'll take a taxi and you'll think.

01:06:11.520 --> 01:06:12.660
I think we're all going to jail.

01:06:12.780 --> 01:06:13.220
That's what I think.

01:06:13.700 --> 01:06:14.280
Monsieur Perron.

01:06:14.420 --> 01:06:14.920
Monsieur Perron.

01:06:15.020 --> 01:06:16.480
You don't seem to realize.

01:06:16.900 --> 01:06:17.260
That...

01:06:17.260 --> 01:06:18.100
That our particular...

01:06:18.100 --> 01:06:18.980
Our particular...

01:06:18.980 --> 01:06:19.420
Gentlemen.

01:06:19.660 --> 01:06:19.880
Gentlemen.

01:06:20.100 --> 01:06:20.300
Gentlemen.

01:06:20.540 --> 01:06:21.340
You don't make sense.

01:06:22.190 --> 01:06:22.830
One at a time.

01:06:22.930 --> 01:06:23.770
Now what is this all about?

01:06:24.050 --> 01:06:25.790
Martin is in jail and I am ruined.

01:06:26.010 --> 01:06:26.170
Yeah.

01:06:26.430 --> 01:06:27.030
He's ruined.

01:06:27.210 --> 01:06:27.930
Martin's in jail.

01:06:27.930 --> 01:06:29.970
Will you kindly keep this echo of yours quiet?

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:30.160
Quiet.

01:06:30.420 --> 01:06:30.820
Quiet!

01:06:31.180 --> 01:06:31.580
Quiet.

01:06:32.720 --> 01:06:35.220
I don't see that either fact interests me.

01:06:35.950 --> 01:06:38.390
You see, your mother has been caught again in a trifling indiscretion.

01:06:38.450 --> 01:06:39.010
May it trifle?

01:06:39.070 --> 01:06:39.950
Attack your daughter again.

01:06:40.800 --> 01:06:41.200
Again?

01:06:41.910 --> 01:06:43.450
The first time was an outrage.

01:06:43.920 --> 01:06:45.360
But if there's a second time...

01:06:45.360 --> 01:06:45.840
It's a triumph!

01:06:46.340 --> 01:06:48.560
Don't try to keep guessing what I'm going to say.

01:06:48.660 --> 01:06:49.420
You mean what you should say?

01:06:49.520 --> 01:06:49.600
Huh?

01:06:50.010 --> 01:06:51.310
Something has got to be done.

01:06:52.070 --> 01:06:54.230
To help you I would do nothing.

01:06:54.580 --> 01:06:55.160
Thank you very much.

01:06:55.450 --> 01:06:58.610
But to keep my daughter's name unblemished I've moved...

01:06:58.610 --> 01:06:59.250
Heaven and Earth!

01:06:59.250 --> 01:06:59.790
No!

01:07:01.560 --> 01:07:03.160
Maybe I cover a little too much territory.

01:07:03.600 --> 01:07:04.380
Gentlemen, gentlemen,

01:07:04.700 --> 01:07:07.040
Marta is in jail and you're ruined.

01:07:32.080 --> 01:07:32.400
Father.

01:07:33.440 --> 01:07:33.780
Well?

01:07:36.880 --> 01:07:37.700
New in the paper.

01:07:38.560 --> 01:07:42.390
Oh, you and Martin still have the headlines.

01:07:43.010 --> 01:07:44.710
Oh, how long do you think they'll keep him in jail?

01:07:45.640 --> 01:07:46.300
Maybe forever.

01:07:47.560 --> 01:07:48.500
Second offense, you know.

01:07:49.890 --> 01:07:54.550
And he's considered dangerous for the entire womanhood of France.

01:07:54.890 --> 01:07:55.790
Oh, that's absurd.

01:07:57.010 --> 01:07:59.510
If he doesn't appear at the theater tonight, he'll never get another chance.

01:08:01.790 --> 01:08:12.170
then it's his career you're interested in yes please stop being an important publisher and

01:08:12.170 --> 01:08:19.120
be an important father but but your excellency gentlemen gentlemen i have had a hundred telegrams

01:08:19.240 --> 01:08:26.010
my phone has been driving me mad all afternoon an army of women so beautiful some so-so

01:08:26.010 --> 01:08:29.970
are now waiting in my ante-room, all demanding his relief.

01:08:30.120 --> 01:08:30.500
Exactly.

01:08:31.140 --> 01:08:34.440
You mean to tell me that you want to be the first man to go down in history to refuse a thousand women?

01:08:34.980 --> 01:08:39.930
No. Yes. To uphold the law, I'd refuse any woman anything.

01:08:41.800 --> 01:08:43.640
Who is this man? He's the Minister of Justice.

01:08:43.900 --> 01:08:45.620
Is he? Are you? Are you really?

01:08:46.160 --> 01:08:46.820
Yes, really.

01:08:47.280 --> 01:08:49.700
Well, hello. How are you? I'll tell you what I'll do.

01:08:50.170 --> 01:08:53.630
You let me have Martin for one month and I'll let you have him for ten years now.

01:08:53.870 --> 01:08:54.710
Very generous offer.

01:08:55.190 --> 01:08:56.760
But entirely without precedent.

01:08:57.310 --> 01:08:58.650
Napoleon, wait for precedent?

01:09:02.010 --> 01:09:03.410
Why don't you confess that you're the monster?

01:09:03.840 --> 01:09:05.340
Why don't you confess that you're an idiot?

01:09:05.480 --> 01:09:06.160
Well, I don't mind.

01:09:06.340 --> 01:09:08.240
Well, all right, then, let's have a good...

01:09:08.420 --> 01:09:11.000
A very fine point has been raised by the idiot.

01:09:11.180 --> 01:09:12.340
I mean, this gentleman here.

01:09:12.650 --> 01:09:14.210
A fine point about Napoleon.

01:09:14.610 --> 01:09:16.390
Like him, I adhere to my decisions.

01:09:17.070 --> 01:09:19.510
In this case, I could do absolutely nothing.

01:09:19.890 --> 01:09:20.290
Nothing?

01:09:20.530 --> 01:09:20.810
Nothing?

01:09:21.260 --> 01:09:21.660
Nothing.

01:09:23.470 --> 01:09:24.280
Pardon me.

01:09:26.250 --> 01:09:26.530
Hello?

01:09:28.970 --> 01:09:29.630
Oh, darling.

01:09:31.340 --> 01:09:32.160
That's my little wife.

01:09:32.700 --> 01:09:34.080
The Empress Josephine.

01:09:34.870 --> 01:09:36.050
Yes, my darling.

01:09:36.410 --> 01:09:36.430
Yes.

01:09:36.760 --> 01:09:40.340
You haven't forgotten about the new review that's opening tonight, have you, darling?

01:09:40.920 --> 01:09:43.690
Oh, oh, darling, I'm sorry.

01:09:43.850 --> 01:09:46.520
An affair of state, this is...

01:09:46.520 --> 01:09:51.580
I know, but I have a new dress.

01:09:51.960 --> 01:09:54.450
Oh, it's an affair of state.

01:09:54.470 --> 01:09:58.120
I want to go, and I have a new dress.

01:09:58.930 --> 01:09:59.870
Oh, oh, my...

01:10:00.060 --> 01:10:08.520
No, my darling. Yes, my darling. No, my darling. Very well, my darling.

01:10:11.780 --> 01:10:13.860
Oh, gentlemen, that really was my little wife.

01:10:16.390 --> 01:10:20.820
You know, on second thought, Napoleon was all so open-minded.

01:10:21.440 --> 01:10:23.980
If I grant your request...

01:10:24.100 --> 01:10:25.120
Oh, thank you so much, George.

01:10:26.240 --> 01:10:29.980
But before I release Martin, you must first get...

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:37.760
The signatures of the chief of police, the inspector of prisons, the keeper of the seals, the registrar, the commissioner.

01:10:46.870 --> 01:10:50.090
Here comes the most important fiancé in Paris, dear.

01:10:57.120 --> 01:10:59.900
But Monique, my sweet, hurry, hurry, you'll be late for the opening.

01:11:01.840 --> 01:11:04.720
Oh, no, no, no. Have you not seen the extra? Just doubt.

01:11:05.260 --> 01:11:07.520
He is being released. Miravilloso.

01:11:09.110 --> 01:11:10.910
Do you understand why you should be so delighted about that?

01:11:11.090 --> 01:11:14.160
Haven't you heard? Mario knows Martin is no actor

01:11:14.160 --> 01:11:15.840
and is just exploiting him.

01:11:16.290 --> 01:11:19.140
As an actor, he will be a colossal flat.

01:11:19.820 --> 01:11:22.400
Tonight, the audience will jeer him off the stage.

01:11:22.880 --> 01:11:25.620
I would have missed that for anything in the world.

01:11:26.570 --> 01:11:27.530
I wouldn't dare enough.

01:11:28.820 --> 01:11:29.980
Yes, all...

01:11:30.120 --> 01:11:32.080
I have been practicing my hiss.

01:11:34.230 --> 01:11:36.690
Fredo, if you so much as that were a hiss,

01:11:37.260 --> 01:11:39.460
one little hiss or even a shush, I'll...

01:11:39.460 --> 01:11:43.310
Now, Monique, if you do not permit me to hiss him,

01:11:43.590 --> 01:11:45.400
I break off the engagements.

01:11:45.820 --> 01:11:48.240
You will? Most likely.

01:11:48.580 --> 01:11:50.950
Come on, Father. You're not dressed for the theatre either.

01:11:52.870 --> 01:11:55.070
I've torn up the... All right.

01:11:55.370 --> 01:11:57.690
I've got four seats for the compliments of the manager.

01:11:57.980 --> 01:11:58.820
Oh, all right.

01:12:25.690 --> 01:12:26.430
I'm not interested.

01:12:26.840 --> 01:12:26.980
What?

01:12:27.540 --> 01:12:28.560
I'm going to stay here.

01:12:28.720 --> 01:12:29.980
Well, after all, the trouble we went...

01:12:30.520 --> 01:12:32.040
Yes, I'm staying here.

01:12:32.400 --> 01:12:34.480
I'm not going to be made a fool of any longer.

01:12:34.970 --> 01:12:38.010
Headlines, photographs, fan mail, my name in lights.

01:12:38.270 --> 01:12:39.810
Not because I'm an actor or a singer,

01:12:39.990 --> 01:12:41.210
but because I'm a freak.

01:12:41.760 --> 01:12:42.960
Well, you tell your newspapers

01:12:42.960 --> 01:12:46.500
that the monster has retired to private life in jail.

01:12:47.930 --> 01:12:48.870
It's that Peleron girl.

01:12:49.830 --> 01:12:50.750
I heard you, Toto.

01:12:51.180 --> 01:12:52.680
Do you think that I'd be interested in a girl

01:12:52.680 --> 01:12:54.560
that allows them to arrest me just because

01:12:54.560 --> 01:12:56.200
I kissed another girl,

01:12:56.340 --> 01:12:57.880
a girl I don't care that much about?

01:12:58.230 --> 01:12:59.470
Oh, then you kissed the wrong girl again.

01:13:00.600 --> 01:13:02.840
That's marvelous. I can just see the headlines tomorrow morning.

01:13:03.440 --> 01:13:04.240
Monster weakened.

01:13:04.560 --> 01:13:05.140
Disappoints audience.

01:13:05.300 --> 01:13:06.560
Refuses to face music.

01:13:06.720 --> 01:13:07.300
Rejects career.

01:13:07.700 --> 01:13:09.180
And Monique will see it at breakfast.

01:13:09.260 --> 01:13:11.060
And she'll turn to Papa Perrin and she'll say,

01:13:11.200 --> 01:13:12.890
I was right to let them arrest him.

01:13:12.950 --> 01:13:15.290
He turned out to be a coward after all.

01:13:19.680 --> 01:13:19.900
Go.

01:13:21.140 --> 01:13:28.640
Play the overture.

01:13:29.220 --> 01:13:29.480
Played it.

01:13:30.280 --> 01:13:32.720
Where's Martin's dress suit?

01:13:33.020 --> 01:13:35.200
Bruno has it on, but I got the veil.

01:13:35.650 --> 01:13:37.930
You will be fortunate if the imposter does not appear.

01:13:38.110 --> 01:13:39.590
Then I shall assume my rightful place.

01:13:39.820 --> 01:13:40.860
The show must go on.

01:13:41.000 --> 01:13:43.240
Yes, and if Martin gets here, those clothes come off.

01:13:43.360 --> 01:13:54.870
They are getting undressed.

01:14:12.130 --> 01:14:13.290
Let me have a program for you.

01:14:14.710 --> 01:14:22.580
It's reserved for Monsieur Martens.

01:14:22.840 --> 01:14:23.780
It's part of the show.

01:14:24.380 --> 01:14:26.950
Oh, I beg your pardon, excuse me.

01:14:27.670 --> 01:14:29.670
Got my wrong teeth.

01:14:30.060 --> 01:14:33.410
On the tanks if you get up there in time.

01:14:33.530 --> 01:14:34.810
On the black eye if you don't.

01:14:34.970 --> 01:14:35.890
Start the show.

01:14:36.130 --> 01:14:36.930
Bring up the curtain.

01:15:42.250 --> 01:15:47.290
And I was lifting, and so I thought to see a movie would be ripping.

01:15:48.040 --> 01:15:53.240
It was so dark there, so nice to park there, especially on one rainy afternoon.

01:15:54.120 --> 01:15:59.920
A lovely stranger sat there beside me, and there was danger but no conscience beside me.

01:16:00.380 --> 01:16:03.020
I squeezed the hand and, oh, it was so grand

01:16:03.020 --> 01:16:05.880
and that lucky rain, rain, rain the afternoon.

01:16:06.810 --> 01:16:10.830
On the screen, there was a scene of love supreme.

01:16:11.500 --> 01:16:16.680
But in between, I caught a glimpse of loveliness divine

01:16:16.680 --> 01:16:19.500
that stole away this heart of mine.

01:16:19.760 --> 01:16:22.600
Believe me, Messa, who could resist her?

01:16:22.840 --> 01:16:26.270
Before I knew what I was doing, I had killed her.

01:16:26.970 --> 01:16:29.260
Glory temper, glory temper.

01:16:30.160 --> 01:16:32.420
brought us together on one rainy afternoon.

01:16:33.640 --> 01:16:37.880
Love has a funny habit, it takes you on nowhere,

01:16:38.550 --> 01:16:42.800
just when you least expect it right beside you there.

01:16:43.360 --> 01:16:47.560
Love came and did I have it, and incidentally,

01:16:48.470 --> 01:16:52.110
look what one rainy afternoon brought.

01:16:54.440 --> 01:16:57.160
The rain was dripping, and I was slipping,

01:16:57.800 --> 01:16:59.900
and so I thought to see a movie would be...

01:17:01.596 --> 01:17:10.916
So dark, so nice to park, especially on one rainy afternoon, a lovely stranger there beside me.

01:17:11.200 --> 01:17:14.120
And there was danger but no conscience there to guide me.

01:17:14.492 --> 01:17:15.872
I see the hand turn.

01:17:15.872 --> 01:17:17.872
No, it was so grand.

01:17:17.872 --> 01:17:20.692
That lucky rave, rave, rave the afternoon.

01:17:21.244 --> 01:17:24.164
Upon the screen, there was a scene.

01:17:24.540 --> 01:17:25.380
Oh, love, supreme.

01:17:26.204 --> 01:17:27.804
But in between...

01:17:28.092 --> 01:17:29.752
I call the glim.

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:32.000
Of loveliness divine

01:17:36.108 --> 01:17:39.108
Believe me, mister, could you resist her?

01:17:39.108 --> 01:17:42.108
Before I knew what I was doing, I guess...

01:17:42.764 --> 01:17:43.524
You're not offended.

01:17:43.784 --> 01:17:43.984
No.

01:17:44.684 --> 01:17:46.544
This story's address

01:17:48.588 --> 01:17:49.288
Reini.
